From cc9d41d9531c881558870825f96c25c1b0985ad8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:43:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(hub-admission): one-statement board census so
 the final hub gate fits its sample; name the refusing stage

The final hub gate runs the whole-host census twice under admission.lock inside a 2.25 s hold. Inside the
gateway each sqlite call, row step and realpath lstat releases the GIL and waits ~one switch interval to get it
back from busy threads; the per-board census made ~80 such handoffs, ~4-8 s over the hub's 10 boards, so every
hub claim since 02:03Z was refused as hub_cpu_unknown before sampling. Read each board's running rows, own-holder
filter and pool receipts in one statement (legacy schemas keep the old path), connect via absolute() not
resolve(), and log the refusing stage with hold_ms/budget_ms for every hub_cpu_unknown branch. CPU limit, window
bounds and cap are unchanged.
